foundation.question_text:
A reciprocal trigonometric graph is shown below on the domain $[0, 2\pi]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
  xmin=-0.3, xmax=6.8, ymin=-4, ymax=4,
  xtick={1.5708, 3.1416, 4.7124, 6.2832},
  xticklabels={$\frac{\pi}{2}$, $\pi$, $\frac{3\pi}{2}$, $2\pi$},
  ytick={-3,-2,-1,1,2,3},
  samples=150, clip=false,
  restrict y to domain=-4:4, unbounded coords=jump,
  axis line style={-{Stealth}}, width=10cm, height=6.5cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=0.26:2.88] {1/sin(deg(x))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=3.40:6.02] {1/sin(deg(x))};
\addplot[dashed, red, domain=0:6.2832] {sin(deg(x))};
\addplot[dashed, gray, domain=-4:4] ({0},{x});
\addplot[dashed, gray, domain=-4:4] ({3.1416},{x});
\addplot[dashed, gray, domain=-4:4] ({6.2832},{x});
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Identify the function shown by the solid blue curve: $y = \operatorname{cosec} x$, $y = \sec x$, or $y = \cot x$.

